&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast, build rockets, and need IT that works. This is an on-site role at our new HQ in Parsdorf. As Working Student IT Helpdesk, you will be the hands-on all-rounder who helps keep our office and shop floor running: laptops, accounts, accessories, printers, meeting rooms, shop floor devices, and whatever blocks people from getting work done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a ticket-forwarding role. You go where the problem is, fix what you can, and make sure our teams have the tools they need to execute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up laptops, accounts, phones, peripherals, and standard workplace equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support users directly in the office and on the shop floor - fast, practical, hands-on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot common IT issues across Windows, Microsoft 365, printers, meeting rooms, networks, and shop floor devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, hand out, collect, and maintain IT equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document simple fixes, recurring issues, and hardware inventory cleanly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the IT team improve basic processes instead of repeating the same manual work forever.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Checklist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled as a student in IT, Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on IT experience and the willingness to fix things, instead of just talking about them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of Windows, Microsoft 365, hardware setup, networks, and common workplace IT issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable walking across office, production, and test areas to solve problems where they happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured, reliable, service-minded, pragmatic, and not afraid to get your hands dirty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English; German is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
